In a previous article, snelling@bnr.ca (Peter Snelling) says:

>It's always annoyed me that some characters have "intrisic" abilities
>which aren't really intrinsics which anyone else could gain.
>
>For example:
>
>- Priests have the ability to determine blessed/uncusred/cursed status
>- Priests and Ninja's have better kicking ability
>- Priests get a shorter prayer time out
>- Archeologists can identify any gems
>- (no others spring to mind)
>
>I think that ANY character class should be able to gain ANY intrinsic,
>even those pseudo intrinsics listed above.
>
	I feel that allowing some characters special abilities
gives variety to the game; without it, every character would
end up playing the same hack/slash type of game. (In fact, they
do, to a large degree) If anything, I would suggest MORE un-earnable 
attributes, not fewer. Perhaps some spells could be cast only by 
priests, and others only by wizards. Healers might be able to tell 
if corpses are fresh and edible or tainted or poisonous. Maybe 
tourists should never find shops that are "closed for inventory." 

